  "result": "I fixed it. The order of the options themselves was fine. The problem was inside each option's entry: the long flag was printed before the short one, like `--verbose, -v` and `--alpha, -a TEXT`, instead of Click's usual `-v, --verbose`.\n\n**Cause:** `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py:319` builds that label. It sorts the flags by prefix length, but with `reverse=True`, so `--` flags came before `-` flags.\n\n**Fix:** I removed `reverse=True`, so the sort runs short-to-long again. Help output now looks like this:\n\n```\n  -a, --alpha TEXT  a\n  -b, --beta TEXT   b\n```\n\nNo existing test covered this, so I added `test_short_options_listed_before_long` to `tests/test_formatting.py`. The full suite passes (1907 passed, 102 skipped). I haven't committed anything.",
